      "id": "0021",
      "src": "/assets/images/main/slider/1313.jpg",
      "title": "Jan Plaza",
      "description": "Jan Plaza is conceived as a poetic cultural space in which light cuts through the dark mass of the earth. Its proportions draw from the historic houses of Kashan, while its narrative is shaped by Persian ideas of love, presence and illumination. Architecture, interior, landscape, graphics and crafted details operate as parts of one story: the movement from concealment toward light.\n\nArchitect and Designer: Jalal Mashhadi Fard · Photography: Diman Studio · Area: 2,600 m² · Completed: 2024",
      "location": "Mashhad / Iran",
      "awards": [
        { "title": "Special Mention — Architecture +Art", "label": "Architizer A+Awards 2025", "url": "https://architizer.com/projects/jan-plaza/" },
